          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Observation skills mean noticing what is actually there instead of what you expect, and they improve through short daily practice such as describing a scene in detail, noticing patterns in a process, asking what is missing and writing brief notes that you review later."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Practise short observation exercises daily, record specific notes and ask what you saw that surprised you."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Proof you can show supports an earlier path to financial freedom."
          }
        ]
